      <h3>why he's my favourite</h3>
      <p>You might not know the name, but the music world does. Jon Bellion writes and produces for the biggest names out there — Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Jason Derulo and plenty more. But it's his own music where it gets ridiculous.</p>
      <p>The man was born for this. Every beat, every lyric, all of it his own. A genius, honestly — unique, jumping across genres, chasing perfection so hard that sometimes you wait years for the next release. Watch his behind-the-scenes videos and you'll see it: how it all comes together in his head.</p>
      <p>And the evolution across the albums, the way the live versions reinvent the songs — his Cove City live set during COVID is a vibe on its own. I've got three of his lyrics tattooed on me: "what if who I hoped to be was always me?", "maybe idk, maybe that's okay", and "insert something really dope right here."</p>
    </div>

